gaGz(){return"Documents"},
gaGu(){return"Terms, privacy and conduct"},
gaGs(){return"DRAFT [pending legal review]\nFor the internal pilot only. These documents are not approved for a service launch."},
gaGt(){return"Pilot draft \u2022 18 November 2026"},
gaGy(){return"1. Terms of use"},
gaGx(){return"BookingDuo connects Customers and Hosts aged 18 or over for meetings in public places in three categories: drinking, travel companionship and interpreting. Provide accurate information and protect your signed-in session.\n\nBefore booking, check the Host, location, time, duration, total fee and displayed cancellation rules. The booking status shows whether an invitation has been accepted and whether a session has started or ended. Food, drinks, tickets and travel are not included in the Host fee.\n\nThe internal pilot uses simulated payments and identity verification. Balances, refunds and payouts in this version are simulations; do not send or receive real money through the test screens.\n\nYou can cancel, report a no-show, request a review or submit a report using the actions and deadlines shown for the booking. Submitting a request does not establish a violation or confirm a completed refund.\n\nThe Licensed guide label requires approval. The Local buddy label does not cover guiding or commentary at tourist sites or selling tours. Launch payment terms, taxes, liability and complaint resolution remain [pending legal review]."},
gaGw(){return"2. Privacy policy"},
gaGv(){return"The test app processes account details, date of birth for age checks, Host profiles, bookings, chat and review content, reports, verification results and simulated transaction information according to the features you use. Do not upload photos or videos of identity cards, passports or driving licences for identity verification.\n\nConsent for each purpose is managed separately in Settings > Privacy. Chat requires filtering consent; review comments have a separate consent purpose. Location is read only when you choose check-in, SOS or Near me. Near me requires separate consent and sends a rounded fix to sort venues. The server does not store that fix. The app does not track in the background. Schedule and emergency-contact sharing need their corresponding consent. Reading this page does not enable any consent.\n\nWhen you send a booking request, the receiving Host can see your display name, your illustrated avatar, the number of earlier bookings for which you held funds as a Customer and your published rating. Phone numbers and personal contact details are not displayed between Customers and Hosts. A person with a valid sharing link can see the permitted schedule details; share only with someone you trust and revoke it when no longer needed. Revocation cannot remove screenshots or copies already kept by a viewer.\n\nYou can edit or export your data, withdraw consent and request account deletion in Settings. The app distinguishes a pending review from a deleted account. Data linked to transaction obligations or incidents may need to be retained for handling; ledger entries and audit records cannot be arbitrarily edited or deleted.\n\nLaunch retention periods, the basis for emergency-contact processing, recipients, the responsible entity and the data-rights contact channel remain [pending legal review]. Do not enter real personal data during the internal trial."},
gavY(){return"Code of conduct"},
gavU(){return"Meet and talk"},
gavT(){return"No physical contact. Do not go elsewhere together after the session."},
gavQ(){return"No pressure to drink"},
gavP(){return"Hosts do not have to drink. A customer is suspended for confirmed pressure to drink during a booking."},
gaw_(){return"Meet in a public place"},
gavZ(){return"Drinking sessions take place at approved partner venues and end by 11:00 PM."},
gavX(){return"Either person can end the session"},
gavW(){return"Tap End session at any time. You do not need to give a reason."},
gavS(){return"Keep communication in the app"},
gavR(){return"Keep phone numbers private and transactions in the app."},
gavV(){return"Internal pilot rules [pending legal review]."},
gaGr(){return"3. Code of conduct"},
gaGq(){return"Respect consent and personal boundaries. Do not harass, threaten, coerce, trade sexual services or use the app for unlawful conduct. Do not post sexual solicitation or misrepresent identity or qualifications.\n\nMeet only at suitable locations allowed by the app. The drinking category requires an approved partner venue. Hosts are not obliged to drink alcohol; never pressure anyone to drink or drive after drinking. Alcohol-brand advertising, donations and virtual gifts are not allowed in the app.\n\nKeep communication in the app. Do not send phone numbers, external contact links or private addresses to bypass safeguards. Chat filtering and warnings operate after you grant processing consent.\n\nReport a profile, booking or message when needed. If you feel unsafe, end the session and use the appropriate incident action. Pilot SOS creates simulated alerts and receipts; it does not guarantee that a real desk or emergency contact has received anything and does not replace real emergency assistance.\n\nAdministrators review information within their permissions and record reasons for decisions. Accepting a report does not establish a violation. The formal enforcement process, decision appeals and support operations remain [pending legal review]."},
